usage: code-review-graph [-h] [-v]
                         {install,init,uninstall,build,update,postprocess,embed,watch,status,forget,visualize,wiki,register,unregister,repos,eval,detect-changes,enrich,dead-code,query,impact,search,flows,flow,communities,community,architecture,large-functions,refactor,serve,mcp,daemon}
                         ...

Persistent incremental knowledge graph for code reviews

positional arguments:
  {install,init,uninstall,build,update,postprocess,embed,watch,status,forget,visualize,wiki,register,unregister,repos,eval,detect-changes,enrich,dead-code,query,impact,search,flows,flow,communities,community,architecture,large-functions,refactor,serve,mcp,daemon}
    install             Register MCP server with AI coding platforms
    init                Alias for install
    uninstall           Safely remove code-review-graph data, configs, hooks,
                        and generated skills
    build               Full graph build (re-parse all files)
    update              Incremental update (only changed files)
    postprocess         Run post-processing on existing graph (flows,
                        communities, FTS)
    embed               Compute vector embeddings for semantic search
    watch               Watch for changes and auto-update
    status              Show graph statistics
    forget              Remove already-parsed files from the graph without a
                        full rebuild
    visualize           Generate interactive HTML graph visualization
    wiki                Generate markdown wiki from community structure
    register            Register a repository in the multi-repo registry
    unregister          Remove a repository from the multi-repo registry
    repos               List registered repositories
    eval                Run evaluation benchmarks
    detect-changes      Analyze change impact against the existing graph
                        (read-only). Does NOT re-parse files — for that, use
                        'update --brief'.
    enrich              Enrich hook input with graph context
    dead-code           Find functions/classes with no callers or test
                        references
    query               Query graph relationships
    impact              Analyze the blast radius of changes
    search              Search graph entities
    flows               List stored execution flows
    flow                Show one stored execution flow
    communities         List graph communities
    community           Show one graph community
    architecture        Show architecture overview
    large-functions     Find oversized graph nodes
    refactor            Preview graph-backed refactors
    serve               Start MCP server (stdio by default, or HTTP on
                        localhost with --http)
    mcp                 Alias for serve
    daemon              Multi-repo watch daemon (start/stop/status/add/remove)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -v, --version         Show version and exit
